  "term": "parent management training",
  "definition": "Parent management training (PMT) is a parent-focused training approach used in the treatment of children with attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder and oppositional defiant disorder. It aims to help parents manage ADHD symptoms and oppositional behavior problems.",
